    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#shaka-zulu-king">Shaka</a> turned a small chiefdom into the strongest state in southeastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#africa">Africa</a> between 1816 and 1828.</li><li>Its power rested on age-regiments (amabutho) of young men bound to the king and on royal control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cattle">cattle</a>.</li><li>The Zulu routed a British force at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-isandlwana">Isandlwana</a> in 1879 but were defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ulundi">Ulundi</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#britain">Britain</a> annexed Zululand in 1887.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Zulu regiments could marry only with the king’s permission, often granted when the men were in their late thirties, giving the king control over new households.</p></aside>
    </section>

